{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EXTERNAL AC VERIFIED via CI (2026-08-19/20). Dispatched the \"Live External Integration\" workflow on main (commit 46b5d60f6fd8615ceb3db21bf02b3b4dc31734da, which includes the landed fix from Gerrit change 1909) — GitHub Actions run 32308848370, job \"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\". The DC harness suite ran against a real, ephemeral Jira Data Center on native amd64 and finished green: 73 passed, 1 xfailed in 5089.10s (1:24:49).\n\nAC#4 evidence — the target live rehearsal PASSED:\n  PASSED tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py::test_unknown_project_skips_and_continues\n\nNOTE on the test name: AC#4 was authored against the original name test_unknown_project_fails_closed. The landed fix RENAMED it to test_unknown_project_skips_and_continues because skip-and-continue (not fail-closed) is the INTENDED multi-project behavior for an unknown/failed mapped project key — a single-project mapping fails closed, but a multi-project run must skip the unknown key and continue the others. The renamed test is the same live rehearsal the AC refers to, and it now passes.\n\nRun URL: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32308848370\nThis is the \"next Live External Integration run\" the AC required, run on main after the fix merged. AC#4 tagged [operator-attested] backed by this concrete CI evidence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787184348662284001,"uuid":"c9655a37-3ba5-4490-b7b9-eafd9fecac8d"}